From a2b3831561700d20be67b74038280a6edb495f5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:10:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Air sound (held): one-shot takes on a pool of the scene's own
 voices, at most 10 begun a frame; off unless the mix asks

For the Mac's Bremen film stall with the sound on (frames alternating about 170 and 6 ms), should its trace show the
game thread making and destroying the takes' voices: every one-shot take was a new audio component (CreateSound2D,
destroyed at its end) and, for a gun's part, a world timer for its cut. Held: it ships only if the trace shows that.

- The pool (mix.json air.voicePool): audio components the scene owns (VoicePool), made as first wanted up to
  `components` and never destroyed, each given take after take once its last has ended. At most `voices` sound at once
  without fading out; past that a take takes the voice of the farthest far take (300 m or more from the eye where it
  is now, not the ridden plane's own, not a big moment), faded over air.limits.cutFade; a far take takes only a voice
  farther off than itself. Each pooled voice carries a generation, and a take is kept as its voice, slot and
  generation (FAirTake), so GunTakes, the muzzle move, GunStop and the cut reach a pooled voice only while it still
  plays that take.
- The cuts: a pooled take's part end is checked each frame (TakesDue) in place of a world timer a take, counted from
  the start of the frame it was asked in, so it falls on the timer's own frame.
- The cap (air.takesPerFrame, air.takesHeldFor): at most 10 takes begun a frame. A far take past it, or finding no
  voice, is held and begun on the first following frame with room, the held before the new, and dropped only once it
  has waited longer than 0.12 s and still finds no room. The ridden plane's own takes, anything within 300 m of the eye
  and big moments are never held, delayed or taken; with the pool full they get a voice of their own, as before. A
  held gun take is kept for its gun when it begins and cut where it would have been; if its gun stops while it waits,
  it is begun and faded at once, as a gun firing for one frame was.
- Loops (the formations' engines, the ridden engine, the far bed) are laid as before: never pooled, held or counted.
- Levels and priorities as they were. With none of the new keys in the mix the scene does what it did: a harness
  compares its calls into the engine with 24b8d1b9's, call for call. mix.json sets voices 96, components 128, 10 a
  frame and 0.12 s, each with its note.
- The 20 s tally line (takes laid on) gains takes pooled, voices made, reused, stolen, held, dropped, and on a voice of
  their own; a line at open gives the numbers.

Not built in Unreal (none here): the changed functions and blocks compiled from their literal text against stand-ins,
g++ and clang++ -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wshadow -Werror, and run against a model of the audio engine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
